earning via  discrete log  right so i think hhl still uses this  amplitude encoding because it assumes  some  input is provided in terms of quantum  states  and this is fundamentally a different  model  from our setting where the only input we  receive  is a set of classical vectors  and we need to find a way to load them  into quantum computers  so i would say that uh this is in a  different input model  and in the classical setting which is  what we are talking about  um sort of it's it is unclear  that heuristic quantum machine learning  algorithms  could in principle solve a hard problem  because the way that they use quantum  computers is not necessarily the most  general way  so our result is sort of solving that  challenge  thank you there's one more question  could you explain the plot on the last  slide in more detail  oh right um  okay um  yeah so the second okay so the first  figure  is the quantum fissure map that was  implemented in this experiment  where this is just a shallow circuit and  of course if you keep the  steps as the same and scale up to many  cubits this is still classically similar  and the second picture is the numerical  simulation of the  quantum kernel estimation routine and  you can see that they are comparing this  quantum fusion map  with rbf which is actually one of the  examples  of classical fissure maps that i just  described before so they can observe a  similar performance  in testing after doing some training and  finally in this  experimental implementation um the  accuracy of course drops because of the  noise  but it's still beyond 60 which is uh  sort of a non-trivial accuracy  okay uh it doesn't seem like there are  any more questions but  thank you again  i think we have some time for the next  one so
 

